{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/481128-transformation-time-limits-in-1e","id":481128,"title":"Transformation Time Limits in 1e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T22:48:44-07:00","id":481128,"title":"Transformation Time Limits in 1e?","content":"The first time I read through Forsaken 1e, I could've sworn I'd read something about werewolves being able to hold most non-human forms indefinitely as they please. But now that I'm going through the book again to confirm this, I've found the time limit that is imposed on the Gauru form (p. 172) but nothing about a time limit or lack thereof on Dalu, Urshal, or Urhan forms. Can anyone help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5569-silverokami","name":"SilverOkami","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T23:00:07-07:00","id":481147,"title":"","content":"They don't explicitly call it out on any page, but the book spells out that all forms are your natural form. The only one with a Time Limit is Gauru, and the effects that your Harmony rating can have on your shifting. So to me it appears that you can chill out forever and a day in any of the other four, but its usually the mindset of the characters that have them sticking with certain forms for tasks.<br /> <br /> Also, walking downtown as a horse-sized wolf probably isn't a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T23:04:47-07:00","id":481149,"title":"","content":"None of the other forms have time limits. It is only the Garou that has a time limit, due to the powerful rage that fills you when you wear that form. If you stay in the form too long, your control slips, and you death frenzy. In 2nd edition, Garou form is accompanied by improved regeneration and combat ability above and beyond its stat adjustments, I recommend that you have a look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T23:46:10-07:00","id":481187,"title":"","content":"Gauru only has a time limit if you want to avoid Death Rage (which, to be fair, would be totally reasonable). You're not forced to shift out of it after a certain amount of time, it's just that the form is so closely tied to the werewolf's inner rage that you can only keep the rage at bay for a limited time while in that form. The fact that you get a &quot;last chance to get off before the express trip to Kuruth town&quot; is just a courtesy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T05:29:55-07:00","id":481277,"title":"","content":"Well, even kuruth will burn out eventually. So there is kind of a time limit even then (made far more explicit in second edition, where it ranges between ten minutes and twelve hours depending on primal urge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T10:56:51-07:00","id":481405,"title":"","content":"I thought that the time limit was due in a large part to the rage literally killing your body. The time limit is that &quot;safe&quot; time your body can handle the power of father wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T11:13:41-07:00","id":481418,"title":"","content":"If that was the case then forcing yourself to stay in it would result in damage and not death rage.<br /> <br /> Really, I think an argument could be made for having the limit be <i>resolve</i> + primal urge, but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T05:37:24-07:00","id":482231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/481128-transformation-time-limits-in-1e?p=481405#post481405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that the time limit was due in a large part to the rage literally killing your body. The time limit is that &quot;safe&quot; time your body can handle the power of father wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's not anime. &quot;Death Rage&quot; is a metaphorical term, because you lose your grip on all stimuli (no conscience, no pain perception, no loyalty, no moral quandaries) - and because you usually kill or get killed in that state of being. That was the rationale in the first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T17:03:29-07:00","id":484039,"title":"","content":"All right! Thank you all for the info!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5569-silverokami","name":"SilverOkami","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}